WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.888
This is the Week 11 working drawing. Open your deck model from Week 9. The drawing is made from it, so if the model changes, the drawing updates.

00:00:10.438 --> 00:00:13.944
Click the + at the bottom left and choose Create Drawing.

00:00:14.494 --> 00:00:24.200
Pick Onshape templates → ANSI → ANSI_A_MM. Choose No views, then OK.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:31.739
Click your part. Set View scale to 1:1, so the drawing is real size. Click to place the front view.

00:00:32.289 --> 00:00:36.144
Move up and click. That's the top view, right above the front view.

00:00:36.694 --> 00:00:40.676
For the right view, open the view menu and choose Projected view.

00:00:41.226 --> 00:00:43.536
Pick the front view, move right, and click.

00:00:44.086 --> 00:00:53.618
Three views: top above front, right beside front. That's third-angle projection, the same layout from Week 2.

00:00:54.168 --> 00:01:02.690
Now dimension. For overall length, use the Maximum dimension tool (Ctrl+M) and pick both rounded ends: 96.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.501
Press D and pick the top and bottom edges: 28 wide.

00:01:08.051 --> 00:01:12.091
Shift+D is the diameter tool. Pick one hole: Ø2.3.

00:01:12.641 --> 00:01:17.320
Now the hole spacing. Pick two holes: 8 mm along the deck,

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:18.915
6 mm across,

00:01:19.465 --> 00:01:23.366
and 42 mm between the trucks. Each size appears once.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:32.612
The fillet adds extra lines. Right-click a view → Tangent edges → Hidden, so you pick the real edges.

00:01:33.162 --> 00:01:37.399
Then dimension the thickness on the right view: 2.5 mm.

00:01:37.949 --> 00:01:48.178
The title block reads properties. Right-click the part → Properties. Fill in the titles, including the hole note: bolt + clearance.

00:01:48.728 --> 00:01:56.344
For the drawing number, right-click the drawing tab → Properties → Part number. Then click Update.

00:01:56.894 --> 00:02:05.706
Check every box: title, hole note, drawing no., mm, 1:1, name, date.

00:02:06.256 --> 00:02:16.473
To turn it in, right-click the drawing tab → Export → PDF. Then trade with a partner: could they build your deck from this page alone?
